# Livestream scheduled-start behavior (optional — every value has a default)
# Install: cp to ~/.config/soundbooth/livestream-schedule.conf and edit
#
# Read by: livestream-autostart.sh (fired by livestream-autostart.timer)
#
# NOTE: the schedule itself (the day/time) does NOT live here — it's the
# timer's OnCalendar=. Change it with:
#     ~/bin/livestream-schedule.sh --set "Sun 09:23"
#     ~/bin/livestream-schedule.sh            # show current + next run
# This file tunes what happens *when the timer fires*.
#
# The camera IP comes from ~/.config/soundbooth/camera.conf (CAMERA_NETWORK_IP);
# don't duplicate it here.

# Optional overrides:

# LIVESTREAM_AUTOSTART_DISABLE=1
#   Suppress scheduled starts while leaving the timer itself enabled. Useful for
#   a week with no service, without having to remember to re-arm the timer after.

# LIVESTREAM_AUTOSTART_REQUIRE_CAMERA=1
#   1 (default) = wait for the program camera to actually deliver a frame before
#   starting the relay. Set 0 to start the stream the moment the timer fires.
#   Leaving this at 1 is strongly preferred: livestream-camera-watch.service ends
#   the stream after ~75s without camera frames, so starting early just produces
#   a stream that comes up and immediately dies.

# LIVESTREAM_AUTOSTART_CAMERA_WAIT_SEC=1200
#   How long to keep waiting for that first frame (default 20 min). Covers the
#   camera being switched on a little after the scheduled time. On timeout the
#   stream is NOT started and a WARNING is logged to the journal.

# LIVESTREAM_AUTOSTART_POLL_SEC=15
#   How often to re-probe the camera while waiting. Matches
#   LIVESTREAM_CAMERA_POLL_SEC in camera.conf.

# LIVESTREAM_AUTOSTART_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SEC=6
#   Per-probe RTSP frame-pull timeout. Ping alone is not trusted — this camera
#   answers RTSP with its encoder off (confirmed 2026-08-30).
